# Service Layer Implementation Patterns

## Architecture Overview

Services contain the **core business logic** of the application and act as the bridge between controllers/handlers and data models. They ensure business rules are centralized and reusable across different transport layers (HTTP API, MCP, GraphQL, etc.).

## Key Principles

### 1. Business Logic Centralization
Services are the **single source of truth** for business rules, data processing, and validation logic.

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT - Business logic in service
async getAllIssues({ category, name, page = 1, limit = 30 }) {
  const issues = await issueModel.findMany(category, name, page, limit);
  const totalIssues = await issueModel.count(category, name);

  return {
    issues,
    total: totalIssues,
    page: Number(page),
    totalPages: Math.ceil(totalIssues / limit), // Business calculation
  };
}

// ❌ WRONG - Business logic in controller/handler
const issues = await issueModel.findMany(filters);
const processed = issues.map(/* processing */); // This belongs in service
```

### 2. Transport Agnostic
Services should **never** contain HTTP-specific logic or MCP-specific formatting. They return pure data structures.

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT - Returns data only
return {
  issues: processedIssues,
  total: totalCount,
  page: Number(page)
};

// ❌ WRONG - HTTP concerns in service
return res.status(200).json(data); // HTTP logic doesn't belong here
```

### 3. Input Validation & Error Handling
Services should validate inputs and throw meaningful errors that transport layers can handle appropriately.

## Standard Service Pattern

### Reference Implementation
See [src/services/issueService.js](mdc:src/services/issueService.js) for the correct pattern (excluding test-only methods like `getMockIssues`).

### Template Structure
```javascript
import { domainModel } from "../models/domainModel.js";

export const domainService = {
  // List/Search with pagination
  async getAll({ filter1, filter2, page = 1, limit = 30 }) {
    // Input validation
    const validatedPage = Number(page);
    const validatedLimit = Number(limit);
    
    // Business logic - data retrieval
    const items = await domainModel.findMany(filter1, filter2, validatedPage, validatedLimit);
    const totalItems = await domainModel.count(filter1, filter2);

    // Business logic - response structure
    return {
      items,
      total: totalItems,
      page: validatedPage,
      totalPages: Math.ceil(totalItems / validatedLimit),
    };
  },

  // Get by ID with validation
  async getById(itemId) {
    if (!itemId) {
      throw new Error("Item ID is required");
    }

    const item = await domainModel.findById(itemId);

    if (!item) {
      throw new Error(`Item with ID ${itemId} not found`);
    }

    return item;
  },

  // Create with validation
  async create(itemData) {
    // Business validation
    if (!itemData || !itemData.name) {
      throw new Error("Unable to create item without required fields");
    }

    // Additional business rules
    if (itemData.name.length < 3) {
      throw new Error("Item name must be at least 3 characters");
    }

    const createdItem = await domainModel.create(itemData);
    return createdItem;
  },

  // Update with validation and data cleaning
  async update(itemId, updateData) {
    if (!itemId) {
      throw new Error("Item ID is required");
    }

    // Business logic - clean and validate update data
    const { name, category, description, ...otherFields } = updateData;
    
    const cleanUpdateData = {
      name,
      category,
      description,
      ...otherFields,
    };

    // Remove undefined/null values if needed
    Object.keys(cleanUpdateData).forEach(key => 
      cleanUpdateData[key] === undefined && delete cleanUpdateData[key]
    );

    const updatedItem = await domainModel.update(itemId, cleanUpdateData);
    return updatedItem;
  },
};
```

## Input Validation Patterns

### Required Field Validation
```javascript
async create(itemData) {
  if (!itemData || !itemData.name) {
    throw new Error("Unable to create item without name");
  }
  
  // Additional required field checks
  if (!itemData.category) {
    throw new Error("Category is required");
  }
}
```

### ID Validation
```javascript
async getById(itemId) {
  if (!itemId) {
    throw new Error("Item ID is required");
  }
  
  // Optional: Format validation
  if (typeof itemId !== 'string' || itemId.trim() === '') {
    throw new Error("Invalid item ID format");
  }
}
```

### Data Type Validation
```javascript
async getAll({ page = 1, limit = 30 }) {
  const validatedPage = Number(page);
  const validatedLimit = Number(limit);
  
  if (isNaN(validatedPage) || validatedPage < 1) {
    throw new Error("Page must be a positive number");
  }
  
  if (isNaN(validatedLimit) || validatedLimit < 1 || validatedLimit > 1000) {
    throw new Error("Limit must be between 1 and 1000");
  }
}
```

## Error Handling Standards

### Meaningful Error Messages
```javascript
// ✅ GOOD - Specific, actionable error messages
throw new Error("Issue ID is required");
throw new Error(`Issue with ID ${issueId} not found`);
throw new Error("Unable to create issue without name");

// ❌ BAD - Generic, unhelpful errors
throw new Error("Error occurred");
throw new Error("Invalid input");
```

### Business Rule Errors
```javascript
async create(issueData) {
  if (issueData.priority === 'critical' && !issueData.assignee) {
    throw new Error("Critical issues must have an assignee");
  }
  
  if (issueData.dueDate && new Date(issueData.dueDate) < new Date()) {
    throw new Error("Due date cannot be in the past");
  }
}
```

## Data Processing Patterns

### Pagination Structure
```javascript
return {
  items: resultArray,
  total: totalCount,
  page: Number(page),
  totalPages: Math.ceil(totalCount / limit),
  hasNextPage: page < Math.ceil(totalCount / limit),
  hasPrevPage: page > 1,
};
```

### Data Transformation
```javascript
async getProcessedItems(filters) {
  const rawItems = await itemModel.findMany(filters);
  
  // Business logic - data processing
  const processedItems = rawItems.map(item => ({
    ...item,
    displayName: `${item.name} (${item.category})`,
    isOverdue: item.dueDate && new Date(item.dueDate) < new Date(),
    statusColor: this.getStatusColor(item.status),
  }));
  
  return processedItems;
}
```

### Aggregation Logic
```javascript
async getStatistics() {
  const allItems = await itemModel.findAll();
  
  return {
    total: allItems.length,
    byStatus: this.groupByStatus(allItems),
    byCategory: this.groupByCategory(allItems),
    recentlyCreated: allItems.filter(item => 
      new Date(item.createdAt) > new Date(Date.now() - 7 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000)
    ).length,
  };
}
```

## What NOT to Include in Services

### ❌ Test-Only Methods
```javascript
// DON'T include mock/test methods in production services
async getMockItems() {
  const mockData = [/* hardcoded test data */];
  await sleep(1000); // Artificial delays for testing
  return mockData;
}
```

### ❌ HTTP-Specific Logic
```javascript
// DON'T include HTTP status codes or response formatting
return res.status(200).json(data);
return { statusCode: 200, body: data };
```

### ❌ Transport-Specific Formatting
```javascript
// DON'T format for specific transports
return {
  content: [{ type: "text", text: JSON.stringify(data) }] // MCP-specific
};
```

## Service Dependencies

### Model Layer Integration
```javascript
import { domainModel } from "../models/domainModel.js";

// Services should primarily interact with models
const items = await domainModel.findMany(filters);
```

### Cross-Service Dependencies
```javascript
import { userService } from "./userService.js";
import { notificationService } from "./notificationService.js";

async create(issueData) {
  // Validate related entities
  if (issueData.assigneeId) {
    await userService.getById(issueData.assigneeId); // Validates user exists
  }
  
  const issue = await issueModel.create(issueData);
  
  // Trigger related business logic
  if (issueData.priority === 'critical') {
    await notificationService.sendAlert(issue);
  }
  
  return issue;
}
```

## Testing Services

Services should be unit tested to verify:
- Input validation logic
- Business rule enforcement
- Data transformation accuracy
- Error handling scenarios
- Cross-service integration

## Common Service Patterns

### CRUD Operations
```javascript
export const crudService = {
  async getAll(filters) { /* list with filtering */ },
  async getById(id) { /* single item retrieval */ },
  async create(data) { /* creation with validation */ },
  async update(id, data) { /* update with validation */ },
  async delete(id) { /* deletion with checks */ },
};
```

### Search & Filter
```javascript
async search({ query, filters, sort, page, limit }) {
  const searchResults = await model.search({
    query,
    filters: this.validateFilters(filters),
    sort: this.validateSort(sort),
    page: Number(page),
    limit: Number(limit),
  });
  
  return this.formatSearchResults(searchResults);
}
```

This service layer pattern ensures your business logic is reusable, testable, and enables seamless integration with multiple transport layers including MCP.

